     "text": "{\"count\":2,\"rationale\":\"u6 can only be reached by passing through every phase in order, so cutting any one phase cut makes u6 unreachable. Phase u2 cannot be cut because op3 has no blocking toggle. Every other phase has two alternative operators, and each operator is blocked by at least one toggle. Cutting such a phase therefore takes one toggle per operator, so 2 toggles. For example, t5 and t6 disable op4 and op5, the only ways to complete u3. No single toggle works, because each one disables only one operator and every blockable phase has a second, independent operator. The minimum is 2.\"}"
